# Cline rules -- witchgame

## Boot order (read at session start, in this order)

1. `docs/instructions.md` -- the canonical rules file. It governs; what
   follows is only its operational summary.
2. `docs/world.md` -- design law. When behavior and design disagree, the
   design docs win and the code is wrong.
3. `docs/PROJECT_MAP.md` -- auto-generated map of every script and function,
   with docstrings.

## Non-negotiables on every `.gd` edit (audited by `build_project_map.py`)

- File header: exactly **3 consecutive `##` lines**, no blank line before
  them. Not 2, not 4.
- Every `func`: exactly **one `##` docstring line** directly above it, at the
  same indent (`@annotations` between the two are tolerated). The docstring is
  the function's API doc: what it does, inputs, return value, invariants the
  caller must know. Vague docstrings degrade every future session.
- Inside function bodies: **single `#` one-liners only.** Never a run of 2+
  consecutive comment lines, never `##` inside a body. Trailing inline
  comments on a code line are fine.
- Palette law: `Color(...)` literals live ONLY in `scripts/render/palette.gd`
  (exempt: `scripts/testing/`). Everywhere else, `Palette` constants.
- Kept conventions: `# -- Section ------...------` banners at class scope; one
  blank line between a docstring's func and the next docstring.

## Gates before you call any change done

1. `python3 build_project_map.py` exits 0 (clean pass writes
   `docs/PROJECT_MAP.md`; the file is generated -- never hand-edit it).
2. The regression suite exits 0 (or run the VS Code task
   "witchgame: regression suite"):

       ~/.var/app/io.github.MakovWait.Godots/data/godot/app_userdata/Godots/versions/Godot_v4_7_2-stable_linux_x86_64/Godot_v4.7.2-stable_linux.x86_64 --headless --path . -s res://scripts/testing/run_all.gd

3. After adding/moving any script with `class_name` (or moving any scripts),
   rescan first -- task "witchgame: Godot class rescan (headless)" or reload
   the project in the open editor -- otherwise headless runs lie.

## Working agreements

- Small, scoped diffs; one concern per change. Nothing is committed and
  nothing is pushed without an explicit human go.
- Design ambiguities: ask, never assume (`docs/world.md` and friends are the
  canonical vision, updateable by the human at any time).
- Memory bank duty: update `docs/` at the end of every working session,
  whenever the human reports a milestone or ruling, and whenever the bank has
  drifted from reality.
